Method &amp; Path Description <code>GET /feedback/?lesson_skill_id=&amp;session_id=&amp;result_flag=</code> Query feedback entries (all filters optional) <code>GET /feedback/{entry_id}</code> One entry (404 if unknown) <code>GET /feedback/metrics/usage?lesson_skill_id=</code> Usage and success/failure/pending counts, overall and per lesson <code>GET /feedback/metrics/success-rate?lesson_skill_id=</code> Success rate (success / decided), overall and per lesson <code>GET /feedback/metrics/failure-rate?lesson_skill_id=</code> Failure rate, overall and per lesson <code>GET /health</code> <code>{"status": "ok"}</code> <pre><code>// GET /feedback/metrics/usage
{
  "by_lesson": {"2b9e…": {"usage_count": 6, "success": 2, "failure": 1, "pending": 0,
                          "success_rate": 0.667, "failure_rate": 0.333}},
  "overall":   {"usage_count": 6, "success": 2, "failure": 1, "pending": 0,
                "success_rate": 0.667, "failure_rate": 0.333}
}
</code></pre>

Strategy Needs LLM How it finds patterns <code>statistical</code> (default) No Counts failure <code>error_code</code>s among task outcomes with <code>status == "failure"</code>, and successful <code>action</code>s among episodes with <code>outcome == "success"</code>. Anything seen at least <code>min_occurrences</code> (2) times becomes a <code>failure_mode</code> or <code>successful_strategy</code> pattern. Confidence = count / total <code>llm_only</code> Yes Sends episodes and outcomes (in chunks of 50) to the LLM and parses a JSON list of patterns <code>clustering_llm</code> Yes Embeds all records, clusters them with KMeans (default 3 clusters), and asks the LLM to summarise each cluster <code>custom_dsl</code> No Runs your own Python <code>extract(dataset) -&gt; list[dict]</code> in a restricted namespace (safe built-ins only; not a hard sandbox) <p>Records the <code>statistical</code> strategy understands:</p> <pre><code>episode     = {"action": "retry_with_backoff", "outcome": "success"}
task_result = {"status": "failure", "error_code": "RATE_LIMIT"}
</code></pre> <p>A custom strategy:</p> <pre><code>from memorygrid_learner.learner import workflows  # registers the built-in strategies
from memorygrid_learner.learner.workflow_runner import WorkflowRunner

script = '''
def extract(dataset):
    slow = [e for e in dataset["episodes"] if e.get("latency_ms", 0) &gt; 2000]
    if len(slow) &lt; 3:
        return []
    return [{"pattern_type": "new_correlation",
             "description": f"{len(slow)} slow episodes this window",
             "confidence": 0.7, "supporting_evidence": slow[:5]}]
'''
runner = WorkflowRunner("custom_dsl", script_source=script)
</code></pre> <p>You can register your own strategy class with <code>WorkflowRunner.register("name", MyStrategy)</code>. The class must subclass <code>WorkflowStrategy</code> and implement <code>async run(dataset) -&gt; list[ExtractedPattern]</code>.</p>
